1
00:00:00,411 --> 00:00:01,863
If you scratch your legs every night,

2
00:00:02,381 --> 00:00:04,456
it may not be only because you skip moisturizer.

3
00:00:05,908 --> 00:00:08,584
At night, skin temperature rises
and cortisol falls,

4
00:00:08,614 --> 00:00:11,013
and that is often cited as a reason
the itch gets worse.

5
00:00:12,616 --> 00:00:14,419
If the front of your shins cracks
and turns white,

6
00:00:14,766 --> 00:00:16,950
dry-skin eczema is one possibility
to consider.

7
00:00:18,438 --> 00:00:21,842
Dry indoor air from heating and frequent
bathing can make it worse.

8
00:00:23,394 --> 00:00:25,869
If the insides of your elbows and knees
keep turning red,

9
00:00:26,241 --> 00:00:28,329
atopic dermatitis is one possibility
to consider.

10
00:00:29,797 --> 00:00:32,674
The itch often comes first,
and the rash follows.

11
00:00:34,225 --> 00:00:36,543
Topical steroids are not
the same as steroid pills.

12
00:00:37,926 --> 00:00:39,918
Apply the ointment you were prescribed
to the area you were told,

13
00:00:40,468 --> 00:00:43,209
in the amount and for the period you were told.

14
00:00:44,775 --> 00:00:46,875
Before bed, moisturize the dry areas,

15
00:00:47,567 --> 00:00:49,638
and don't cover up so warmly
that you sweat.
